        <name>operator++</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::utils::double_list_iterator::operator++</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Pre-increment operator. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>Reference to the incremented iterator.</para>
</simplesect>
The pre-increment operator (<computeroutput>operator++</computeroutput>) advances the iterator to the next node in the list. It updates the internal node pointer to point to the node returned by the current node&apos;s <computeroutput>next()</computeroutput> method. This allows the iterator to traverse the list in the forward direction, following the linked structure. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
