        <argsstring>(int)</argsstring>
        <name>operator++</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::utils::double_list_iterator::operator++</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Post-increment operator. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>Iterator before increment.</para>
</simplesect>
The post-increment operator (<computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1utils_1_1double__list__iterator_1a60ce68c08d226be1b5ff5bc92e21a4fc" kindref="member">operator++(int)</ref></computeroutput>) advances the iterator to the next node in the list, but returns a copy of the iterator as it was before the increment. This allows iteration logic that requires access to the current element before moving to the next one, following the standard C++ iterator semantics for post-increment. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
