        <briefdescription>
<para>Post-decrement operator. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>Iterator before decrement.</para>
</simplesect>
The post-decrement operator (<computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1utils_1_1double__list__iterator_1a1bc00178e8a6da8c816716236fd60be1" kindref="member">operator--(int)</ref></computeroutput>) moves the iterator to the previous node in the list, but returns a copy of the iterator as it was before the decrement. This enables iteration logic that requires access to the current element before moving backward, following the standard C++ iterator semantics for post-decrement. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
