        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>Pointer to the value pointed to by the iterator.</para>
</simplesect>
The pointer access operator (<computeroutput>operator-&gt;</computeroutput>) allows the iterator to provide direct access to the value pointed to by the iterator, mimicking the behavior of a raw pointer. Internally, it calls <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1utils_1_1double__list__iterator_1a4dda1a12bf05e974cc3e6394f28302a0" kindref="member">get_pointer()</ref></computeroutput>, which computes and returns a pointer to the underlying value or object associated with the current node in the list. </para>
